    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our definitive anchor, boasting an elite 81.88 score. Facing Hancock, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and an favorable dynamic platoon advantage. While the opposing battery has a moderate xERA, the combination of his #2 lineup spot and his ability to contribute across all five categories\u2014particularly the scarcity of speed\u2014makes him the mandatory cornerstone of today\u2019s offensive strategy. Similarly, **Miguel Andujar** and **Jackson Merrill** project as high-ceiling plays against Andrew Abbott; despite the uncertainty of the \"Lineup Pending\" tag, the weak SP_xERA of 4.76 for the opposition provides a favorable environment for them to exceed their base projections.\n\nThe optimization process was most contentious regarding our middle infield depth. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** cleared the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold by a hair, aided by a projected wind-out scenario at his home park, securing his spot over **Nasim Nunez**. While **Nasim Nunez** offered value, his projected #8 spot in the order coupled with the elite pop-time of the opposing catcher penalized his utility score, ultimately pushing him to the bench. We are also wary of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who draws a difficult assignment against S\u00e1nchez. His score of 56.35 is dragged down by the opponent's 2.74 xERA, making him a marginal play; however, his #3 lineup position keeps him in the starting nine as we chase volume in our counting categories.\n\nRisk management remains a priority for the Waves as we navigate several pending lineups and the IL status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and the rest day for **Kyle Tucker**. While **Coby Mayo** sits on the lower end of our active spectrum at 48.28, he remains in the lineup due to the lack of viable alternatives currently available on the bench. We will monitor the confirmed lineups for **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Miguel Andujar**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Nolan Schanuel** closely; if these players shift significantly lower in their respective batting orders, we may see their efficiency scores dip, potentially triggering a reassessment of our strategy to preserve game caps for higher-leverage matchups later in the week.",
